 -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(-5,5),$ $(-3,3).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/cf/cf336b4522756131aeb6dd9bc48ada6f8b255526b6ae20120dcf40f155b1b95c.png)"] [:db/cas 17592186275179 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,3)$, $(-2,0)$ and $(2,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(8,-16)$\n- **II.** $(-6,12)$\n- **III.** $(8,16)$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,3)$, $(-2,0)$ and $(2,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(8,-16)$\n- **II.** $(-6,12)$\n- **III.** $(8,16)$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186275179 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,6)$, $(-6,12)$ and $(8,-16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,6)$, $(-6,12)$ and $(8,-16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""] [:db/cas 17592186275180 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,-1)$, $(1,0)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n- **I.** $(-1,2)$\n- **II.** $(-3,12)$\n- **III.** $(7,-12)$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,-1)$, $(1,0)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n- **I.** $(-1,2)$\n- **II.** $(-3,12)$\n- **III.** $(7,-12)$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186275180 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 12 & 2 & -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,12)$, $(-1,2)$ and $(7,-14).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I  only.\"" "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 12 & 2 & -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,12)$, $(-1,2)$ and $(7,-14).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I  only.\""] [:db/cas 17592186275181 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,0)$, $(0,-3)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(12,-24)$\n- **II.** $(8,16)$\n- **III.** $(2,-4)$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,0)$, $(0,-3)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(12,-24)$\n- **II.** $(8,16)$\n- **III.** $(2,-4)$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186275181 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 12 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -24 & 16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,-4)$, $(12,-24)$ and $(-8,16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 12 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -24 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,-4)$, $(12,-24)$ and $(-8,16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""] [:db/cas 17592186275182 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,3),(0,-2),$ and $(4,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(-11,3)$\n- **II.** $(-5,15)$\n- **III.** $(18,-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,3),(0,-2),$ and $(4,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(-11,3)$\n- **II.** $(-5,15)$\n- **III.** $(18,-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186275182 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & -6 & -5 \\\\ -33 & 18 & 15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(11,-33)$, $(-6,18)$ and $(-5,15).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -6 & -5 \\\\ -33 & 18 & 15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(11,-33)$, $(-6,18)$ and $(-5,15).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""] [:db/cas 17592186275183 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,1),(0,0)$ and $(2,2)$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$  \n- **I.** $(6,-18)$\n- **II.** $(-5,-20)$\n- **III.** $(12,-24)$\n\nSelect all that apply." "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\en